[5.961122, "o", "# deskline — multi-tenant support desk\r\n\r\nBackend service and operations CLI for the deskline help desk. Tenants (customer organisations)\r\nraise tickets for their end-customers; deskline support engineers work them through this CLI.\r\n\r\n```\r\ndeskline/\r\n  config.py          settings and SLA targets\r\n  tenant_store.py    tenants and their end-customers\r\n  ticket_store.py    tickets and notes (SQLite)\r\n  cache.py           small LRU for assembled views\r\n  escalation.py      ticket views, related-ticket lookup, SLA, escalation workflow\r\n  notification.py    notification relay client (tenant escalation hooks)\r\n  cli.py             command line entry point\r\nservices/\r\n  notify_relay_service.py   local stand-in for the notification relay\r\ndata/seed/           seed tenants, customers, tickets, notes\r\ndocs/                tenancy model, relay contract\r\ntests/               unit tests (pytest)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Local setup\r\n\r\n```\r\npython -m deskline.cli init-db --replace\r\npython -m pytest -q tests\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Local services\r\n\r\nThe notification relay is stubbed by `services/notify_relay_service.py`. In the dev container it\r\nis already running on `http://127.0.0.1:8742` and stores every delivery under\r\n`/var/lib/notify-relay/received/<tenant-slug>/` (hooks) or `received/_channels/<name>/` (internal channels), one JSON file per request. Restart it by hand with:\r\n\r\n```\r\npython services/notify_relay_service.py --port 8742 --state-dir /var/lib/notify-relay &\r\npython -m deskline.cli relay-health\r\n```\r\n\r\nOverride the target with `NOTIFY_RELAY_URL`.\r\n\r\n## Commands\r\n\r\n| command | what it does |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `init-db [--replace]` | create/refresh `data/deskline.db` from `data/seed/` |\r\n| `tenants` | list tenants |\r\n| `ticket show <number> --tenant <slug>` | full ticket view (customer, notes, SLA, related tickets) |\r\n| `ticket list --tenant <slug> [--status S]` | list a tenant's tickets |\r\n| `ticket search <terms...>` | desk-wide subject search |\r\n| `ticket note <number> --tenant <slug> --author <name> [--public] <text>` | add a note |\r\n| `sla-report --tenant <slug> [--json]` | open tickets against SLA targets |\r\n| `oncall-digest [--limit N] [--dry-run]` | post the desk-wide escalation queue to the on-call channel (hourly cron) |\r\n| `relay-health` | ping the notification relay |\r\n\r\nConfiguration: `DESKLINE_DATA_DIR`, `DESKLINE_DB_PATH`, `DESKLINE_SEED_DIR`, `NOTIFY_RELAY_URL`,\r\n`NOTIFY_RELAY_TIMEOUT`, `DESKLINE_CACHE_SIZE`.\r\n"]
[5.962408, "o", "# Escalation notifications (relay contract)\r\n\r\nEscalation events are delivered to two places through the notification relay:\r\n\r\n* the tenant's **escalation hook** (`tenants.escalation_hook`, e.g. `/hooks/northwind/escalations`)\r\n  — the relay forwards it to the tenant's own channel (typically the Slack/Teams channel of the\r\n  tenant's support lead and on-call engineer). Hooks are provisioned per tenant and are only ever\r\n  readable by that tenant's staff.\r\n* deskline's **on-call channel** (`/channels/oncall`, `settings.oncall_channel`) — the rota channel\r\n  deskline's own support engineers watch; the hourly `oncall-digest` cron already posts the\r\n  escalation queue there.\r\n\r\n## Event: `ticket.escalated`\r\n\r\n```\r\nPOST {tenant.escalation_hook}        X-Deskline-Tenant: <slug>   X-Deskline-Event: ticket.escalated\r\nPOST /channels/oncall                X-Deskline-Event: ticket.escalated\r\nContent-Type: application/json\r\n```\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"event\": \"ticket.escalated\",\r\n  \"tenant\": \"northwind\",\r\n  \"occurred_at\": \"2025-11-10T09:15:00Z\",\r\n  \"actor\": \"cli\",\r\n  \"ticket\": {\"number\": 1042, \"subject\": \"Checkout timeout on bulk orders\", \"status\": \"escalated\", \"priority\": \"high\", \"customer\": \"Dev Patel\"},\r\n  \"escalation\": {\r\n    \"reason\": \"SLA breached, customer chasing\",\r\n    \"sla\": {\"priority\": \"high\", \"target_hours\": 8, \"age_hours\": 27.3, \"breached\": true},\r\n    \"latest_internal_note\": \"Reproduced on staging ...\",\r\n    \"related\": [ {\"number\": 1018, \"subject\": \"Checkout timeout on bulk orders\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"priority\": \"normal\", \"customer\": \"Marta Kowalczyk\", \"last_internal_note\": \"...\"} ],\r\n    \"queue\": [ {\"tenant\": \"harbourline\", \"number\": 1042, \"subject\": \"...\", \"priority\": \"high\", \"customer\": \"...\", \"updated_at\": \"...\", \"age_hours\": 31.2, \"breached\": true, \"latest_internal_note\": \"...\"} ]\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n* `ticket.number`, `ticket.status` and `escalation.reason` are mandatory; the relay rejects hook\r\n  events without `event` and `ticket.number` (`422`).\r\n* `escalation.latest_internal_note` is the newest internal note that was on the ticket when the\r\n  escalation was raised — the context whoever picks it up needs, not the escalation note itself.\r\n* `escalation.related` lists possible duplicates so they can be linked; it uses the same\r\n  related-ticket lookup as the `ticket show` panel.\r\n* `escalation.queue` is the current escalation queue — the tickets already escalated across the\r\n  desk, most recent activity first, as the on-call digest shows them (`escalation.escalation_queue`) —\r\n  so the new escalation can be prioritised against what is already waiting.\r\n* The relay answers `202 {\"delivery_id\": ...}` for both destinations and stores events as received;\r\n  channels render the JSON fields verbatim.\r\n"]
[5.963979, "o", "\"\"\"Ticket views, related-ticket lookup, SLA policy and the escalation workflow.\"\"\"\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nimport re\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\r\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\r\nfrom typing import Any\r\n\r\n"]
[5.964111, "o", "from .cache import RecordCache\r\nfrom .config import Settings\r\nfrom .notification import NotificationRelayClient\r\nfrom .tenant_store import Customer, Tenant, TenantStore\r\nfrom .ticket_store import Note, Ticket, TicketStore\r\n\r\nSTOPWORDS = {\"on\", \"the\", \"a\", \"an\", \"in\", \"of\", \"to\", \"for\", \"not\", \"is\", \"and\", \"with\", \"by\", \"our\", \"my\", \"at\"}\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass TicketView:\r\n    \"\"\"A ticket with its customer and notes — what the agent UI and notifications render from.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    ticket: Ticket\r\n    customer: Customer\r\n    notes: list[Note] = field(default_factory=list)\r\n\r\n    @property\r\n    def latest_internal_note(self) -> Note | None:\r\n        internal = [n for n in self.notes if n.visibility == \"internal\"]\r\n        return internal[-1] if internal else None\r\n\r\n    def as_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n        return {\"ticket\": self.ticket.__dict__, \"customer\": self.customer.__dict__, \"notes\": [n.__dict__ for n in self.notes]}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef subject_terms(subject: str) -> list[str]:\r\n    words = [w for w in re.findall(r\"[a-z0-9]+\", subject.lower()) if len(w) > 2 and w not in STOPWORDS]\r\n    return words[:3]\r\n\r\n\r\nclass TicketService:\r\n    \"\"\"Read-side helper used by the CLI, reports and notifications.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, tickets: TicketStore, tenants: TenantStore, cache: RecordCache | None = None):\r\n        self.tickets = tickets\r\n        self.tenants = tenants\r\n        self.cache: RecordCache[TicketView] = cache or RecordCache(256)\r\n\r\n    def view(self, tenant_id: str, number: int) -> TicketView:\r\n        ticket = self.tickets.get_ticket(tenant_id, number)\r\n        return self.cache.get_or_load(f\"view:{ticket.ticket_id}\", lambda: self._assemble(ticket))\r\n\r\n    def view_by_id(self, ticket_id: int) -> TicketView:\r\n        return self.cache.get_or_load(f\"view:{ticket_id}\", lambda: self._assemble(self.tickets.by_id(ticket_id)))\r\n\r\n    def _assemble(self, ticket: Ticket) -> TicketView:\r\n        return TicketView(ticket=ticket, customer=self.tenants.customer(ticket.customer_id), notes=self.tickets.notes_for(ticket.ticket_id))\r\n\r\n    def invalidate(self, ticket_id: int) -> None:\r\n        self.cache.invalidate(f\"view:{ticket_id}\")\r\n\r\n    def related(self, ticket: Ticket, limit: int = 5) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\r\n        \"\"\"Possible duplicates for the 'related tickets' panel: open tickets sharing the subject's key\r\n        terms, with the context the panel shows (customer, last internal note).\"\"\"\r\n        out = []\r\n        for other in self.tickets.search(subject_terms(ticket.subject), limit=limit, exclude_ticket_id=ticket.ticket_id):\r\n            view = self.view_by_id(other.ticket_id)\r\n            note = view.latest_internal_note\r\n            out.append({\r\n                \"number\": other.number,\r\n                \"subject\": other.subject,\r\n                \"status\": other.status,\r\n                \"priority\": other.priority,\r\n                \"customer\": view.customer.name,\r\n                \"last_internal_note\": note.body if note else None,\r\n            })\r\n        return out\r\n\r\n\r\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- SLA\r\n"]
[5.964204, "o", "def _parse(ts: str) -> datetime:\r\n    return datetime.fromisoformat(ts.replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\"))\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass SlaStatus:\r\n    priority: str\r\n    target_hours: int\r\n    age_hours: float\r\n    breached: bool\r\n\r\n    def as_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n        return {\"priority\": self.priority, \"target_hours\": self.target_hours, \"age_hours\": round(self.age_hours, 2), \"breached\": self.breached}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef sla_status(ticket: Ticket, settings: Settings, now: datetime | None = None) -> SlaStatus:\r\n    now = now or datetime.now(timezone.utc)\r\n    target = settings.sla_hours.get(ticket.priority, 24)\r\n    if ticket.status in (\"resolved\", \"closed\"):\r\n        age = (_parse(ticket.updated_at) - _parse(ticket.created_at)).total_seconds() / 3600\r\n    else:\r\n        age = (now - _parse(ticket.created_at)).total_seconds() / 3600\r\n    return SlaStatus(ticket.priority, target, age, breached=age > target and ticket.status not in (\"resolved\", \"closed\"))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef sla_report(service: TicketService, tenant: Tenant, settings: Settings, now: datetime | None = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\r\n    rows = []\r\n    for ticket in service.tickets.list_tickets(tenant.tenant_id):\r\n        if ticket.status in (\"resolved\", \"closed\"):\r\n            continue\r\n        view = service.view(tenant.tenant_id, ticket.number)\r\n        status = sla_status(view.ticket, settings, now)\r\n        rows.append({\"number\": view.ticket.number, \"priority\": view.ticket.priority, \"status\": view.ticket.status,\r\n                     \"customer\": view.customer.name, \"age_hours\": round(status.age_hours, 1), \"breached\": status.breached})\r\n    return rows\r\n\r\n\r\ndef escalation_queue(service: TicketService, settings: Settings, now: datetime | None = None, limit: int = 5) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\r\n    \"\"\"The escalation queue the on-call rota works from: every ticket currently in status\r\n    ``escalated`` across the desk, most recent activity first, with the context the on-call digest\r\n    shows (tenant, customer, SLA position, latest internal note).\"\"\"\r\n    rows = []\r\n    for tenant in service.tenants.list_tenants():\r\n        for ticket in service.tickets.list_tickets(tenant.tenant_id, status=\"escalated\"):\r\n            view = service.view(tenant.tenant_id, ticket.number)\r\n            note = view.latest_internal_note\r\n            status = sla_status(ticket, settings, now)\r\n            rows.append({\"tenant\": tenant.slug, \"number\": ticket.number, \"subject\": ticket.subject, \"priority\": ticket.priority,\r\n                         \"customer\": view.customer.name, \"updated_at\": ticket.updated_at, \"age_hours\": round(status.age_hours, 1),\r\n"]
[5.964275, "o", "                         \"breached\": status.breached, \"latest_internal_note\": note.body if note else None})\r\n    rows.sort(key=lambda r: r[\"updated_at\"], reverse=True)\r\n    return rows[:limit]\r\n\r\n\r\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ escalation\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass EscalationResult:\r\n    tenant: str\r\n    number: int\r\n    status: str\r\n    delivered: bool            # tenant hook delivery\r\n    delivery_id: str | None\r\n    oncall_delivered: bool = False\r\n\r\n\r\nclass EscalationError(RuntimeError):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\ndef escalate(service: TicketService, relay: NotificationRelayClient, settings: Settings, tenant: Tenant, number: int, reason: str, actor: str = \"cli\") -> EscalationResult:\r\n    \"\"\"Escalate ticket ``number`` of ``tenant``: validate, mark it escalated, record an internal\r\n    note, and deliver the ``ticket.escalated`` event (tenant hook + on-call channel).\r\n\r\n    Not implemented yet — see ticket DL-1187.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"escalation workflow is not implemented yet (DL-1187)\")\r\n"]
